WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:01.668 line:71%
In the United States,

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.878 line:76%
people actually own
their own images

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:06.715
and it's a form
of intellectual property.

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:10.468
So, typically the question of
what is my image

00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:12.387
is a common sense question.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.556
But, once AI gets into the
picture,

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:17.350
the question of, what is me?
What is my image?

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.477
What is the transformation
of my image,

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:22.230
that is an original work
becomes very puzzling.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.150
In the particular context
that we see it now coming up

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.987
in the strikes in Hollywood,
something even more difficult

00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:31.281
is at stake.

00:00:31.322 --> 00:00:33.283
So if I own my image,

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:37.746
what happens in the world of
movies is that actors

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:41.082
by contract, sign away the
property in their image

00:00:41.082 --> 00:00:42.709
to someone making a movie.

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:45.795
Now the question is,
what do they own?

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:49.048
If, by AI, I can make a
whole new movie

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.842
in which Tom Cruise is saying

00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:53.845
new lines and doing things
he never did in the movie

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:58.224
did Tom Cruise sign away
his rights when he signed

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:02.353
away the rights to his
image in that movie or not?

00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:04.981
AI requires us to begin
to rethink

00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:07.859
exactly what are the parameters
of the property right

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:10.487
and how they have
to be protected by contract.

00:01:10.487 --> 00:01:13.865
And of course, the strike is
about what the contractual terms

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:16.034
the standard terms
will be in the industry.

00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:18.328
This is a turning point in law.

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:21.039
But how much difference
it will make in the real world

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:22.290
no one really can guess.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.336
Predictions range on the one
hand from the apocalyptic,

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:28.505
This is the terminator,
when AI develops

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:30.340
its own self consciousness

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:34.886
to it's really just a toaster
that is more complicated

00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:38.014
than our old toasters and
anything in between these

00:01:38.014 --> 00:01:38.848
two extremes.

